# The coefficients of the product of two polynomials of 2-limb coefficients that the program
# supplies (milestone2.md, "sum, dot, axpy, convolution": conv_k): conv_2 with the coefficients by
# dot_2_entry, whose step guards the limbs of both factors (rule R3, the factors of a fused
# operation: architecture.md). conv_2's step only multiplies the coefficients, but mul_2_2 takes
# them as factors of fused operations whose addends are not zero: a compiler that sees one
# polynomial to hold ones may fuse a product the program stored into the other into them (measured
# in the convolution of one limb, never in this one). Four additions more per term, and the
# statement of conv_2 holds of the values in the arrays whatever the compiler does. Its claims are
# those of conv_2.
fold:          conv_2_entry
arrays:        supplied x = x0 x1, supplied y = y0 y1
coefficients:  dot_2_entry
state:         mask finite
combine:       finite = and(finite, finite)
orders:        sequential
writes:        z = z0 z1
check:         fold_finish_2
finish:        none
value:         x*y
requires:      canonical x
requires:      canonical y
ensures:       coefficients z
ensures:       finite_or_nan z flag=finite
min_precision: 4
theorem:       proofs/theories/FoldConv.v
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeFoldConv.v
terms_theorem: proofs/theories/FoldConv.v
status:        proved
domain:        extended
source:        dot_2_entry on the terms of each coefficient: Higham's bound for summation over any tree, through dot_2_entry
license:       bound: published; proof: MIT
